WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.169
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.337
-Thank you, Franny.

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:06.606
Can you say it?
Franny's younger than you.

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:08.307
How can -- she can say it
and you can't?

00:00:08.307 --> 00:00:10.342
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:10.342 --> 00:00:12.545
-Oh, Winnie, thank you so much.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:13.880
We have a great show tonight.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.748
All new.
-Starring Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:15.748 --> 00:00:17.450
-Oh!
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.518
You never said that before.

00:00:19.518 --> 00:00:21.821
Uh-oh. Do you have anything else
you want to say?

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:23.957
-Poopy face?

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:27.060
-Let's just start the show.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.463
-♪ We in the house ♪

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:33.700
-Tonight, join Jimmy
and his guests...

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.001
Ricky Gervais...

00:00:36.001 --> 00:00:37.370
Billy Porter...

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.405
musical guest The Lumineers...

00:00:39.405 --> 00:00:42.208
and the legendary Roots crew.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:43.977
It's "The Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:45.844
-♪ We in the house, y'all ♪

00:00:45.844 --> 00:00:48.281
And now here's Jimmy.

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:51.250
-Hi, everybody. Welcome to "The
Tonight Show: At Home Edition."

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:52.518
My name is Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:52.518 --> 00:00:54.520
I'm so happy to have you guys
watching the show.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.790
It's Tuesday today,
and Tuesday I say

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:02.295
is just one day closer
to Friday, isn't it, though?

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:04.397
It's definitely not yesterday.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.432
It is -- And it's
not quite tomorrow.

00:01:06.432 --> 00:01:07.633
It's almost, though.
It's almost tomorrow.

00:01:07.633 --> 00:01:09.335
It's basically Wednesday.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.604
Let's just act like it's
Wednesday. But it's Tuesday.

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:13.639
It's great. Monday was great.

00:01:13.639 --> 00:01:16.242
Done. Forward. Onward, upward.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:17.743
That's what we're doing, okay?

00:01:17.743 --> 00:01:19.845
We're in this together.
Let's make this work.

00:01:19.845 --> 00:01:21.313
Thanks for watching, everybody.

00:01:21.313 --> 00:01:24.616 line:0%
Hey, we're working with --
Salesforce really stepped up.

00:01:24.616 --> 00:01:28.822 line:0%
So any donation you make
to World Central Kitchen, okay,

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:32.491 line:0%
Salesforce will match it
up to $250,000.

00:01:32.491 --> 00:01:34.193 line:0%
That's maje.
All you have to do --

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:36.462 line:0%
There's words
on the back of this.

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:39.899 line:0%
Text "Meals" to 80100.

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:42.601 line:0%
And then that will be --

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:44.270
There's something else
on the back of this. Sorry.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.540
-What is it?

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.641
-I don't know.
It's something for you.

00:01:49.641 --> 00:01:51.177
-[ Laughs ]
-Sorry about that.

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:52.745
Winnie drew on the back.
-A love note?

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.079
-It's a love note.

00:01:54.079 --> 00:01:56.515
This is not my handwriting so --
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:56.515 --> 00:01:58.083
Something you want to tell me?
-Interesting.

00:01:58.083 --> 00:01:59.586
-Yeah, it is interesting.

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:02.454
Okay, so, alright, that is that.

00:02:02.454 --> 00:02:04.156
We have a good show tonight.
We'll get to that.

00:02:04.156 --> 00:02:05.691
But first, let's get
to some jokes.

00:02:05.691 --> 00:02:08.026
Guys, it is week seven
of the quarantine,

00:02:08.026 --> 00:02:10.763
and we're running out of ways
to entertain the kids.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.332
Today, my wife and I
told the kids

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:15.601
to go outside and try
to find Kim Jong-un.

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:17.036
Rumors continue to swirl

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:20.006
about whether Kim Jong-un
is dead or alive.

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:21.674
It's crazy. Who knew Kim Jong-un

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:26.245
would turn into this
generation's Tupac, you know?

00:02:26.245 --> 00:02:29.415
Yesterday, President Trump said
he knows Kim Jong-un's condition

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:31.984
but can't talk about it now.

00:02:31.984 --> 00:02:33.886
In response,
Trump's entire staff

00:02:33.886 --> 00:02:38.057
told him to pretend
the coronavirus is Kim Jong-un.

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:39.692
But today, South Korean
officials said

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:42.361
they know the whereabouts
of Kim Jong-un.

00:02:42.361 --> 00:02:45.431
Yeah, they think he's developing
his new rocker persona,

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:48.067
Chris Jong-Gaines.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.335
Could be.

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:50.937
This is nice. I saw that
Facebook and Instagram

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:54.407
are holding a big multi-hour
graduation ceremony

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:57.076
for the entire class of 2020.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:58.945
Sounds cool until they start
reading the names

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:02.514
of everyone graduating
this year.

00:03:02.514 --> 00:03:05.652
Aaron Aaronson.

00:03:08.287 --> 00:03:11.690
Aaron Aaronton.

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:15.394
[ Laughs ]

00:03:15.394 --> 00:03:18.698
Aaron Aaronwon.

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:24.337
A virtual graduation will
feature appearances by Oprah,

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:27.106
Miley Cyrus, Lil Nas X,

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:30.376
and former Ohio governor
John Kasich.

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:35.514
Kids were like, "OMG, former
Ohio governor John Kasich!

00:03:35.514 --> 00:03:39.519
Are you kidding me?"

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:42.321
I read that a Girl Scout's
branch just received federal aid

00:03:42.321 --> 00:03:45.024
to make up
for lost cookie sales.

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:47.259
Yep, the quarantine
has been tough on Girl Scouts.

00:03:47.259 --> 00:03:49.796
So if you can get
some Girl Scout cookies,

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:51.464
please order some.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:54.566
But also to try and boost sales,
the Girl Scouts are releasing

00:03:54.566 --> 00:03:57.236
some new
limited edition flavors.

00:03:57.236 --> 00:04:00.806
For instance, there is
Used-to-be-Thin Mints.

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:03.342
Then there's Tag-Alones.

00:04:03.342 --> 00:04:07.346
There's also Do-Si-Don't
Touch Your Face.

00:04:07.346 --> 00:04:10.316
Then there's Zoomacaroons.

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:14.153
And, of course,
Presidential Bleach Bites.

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:18.257
Next, there's S'more Time
Homeschooling your Kids.

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:21.360
Who couldn't use that, huh?
There's also

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.929
I-think-I'm-about-to
Ginger Snaps.

00:04:23.929 --> 00:04:27.734
And, of course, their
best seller, Liquor-Doodles.

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:30.236
Good luck, girls.
They all sound like winners.

00:04:30.236 --> 00:04:32.338
Listen to this.
I read that secret salons

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:34.674
are now opening up
around the country.

00:04:34.674 --> 00:04:37.243
100 years ago, the mob
was operating speakeasies.

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:40.413
Now they're like,
"You need a perm?

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:43.949
You should go to this address.
Okay?

00:04:43.949 --> 00:04:47.319
Okay, we got manis,
we got pedis.

00:04:47.319 --> 00:04:50.789
What do you want? Mani/pedi?"

00:04:50.789 --> 00:04:52.091
This isn't good.
In North Carolina,

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:55.261
a dog has tested positive
for COVID-19.

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:57.897
So if you thought teaching
your dog how to shake was hard,

00:04:57.897 --> 00:05:02.568
good luck teaching him
how to elbow bump instead.

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:05.671
Do dogs have elbows?

00:05:05.671 --> 00:05:08.341
And finally, I saw
that U.P.S. is using drones

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:12.044
to deliver medication to a
retirement community in Florida.

00:05:12.044 --> 00:05:14.147
So don't panic
if you see a bunch of old people

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:18.284
screaming at the sky,
"Where's my pills?"

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:20.085
That is our monologue,
everybody.

00:05:20.085 --> 00:05:22.354
Oh, man, we have a good show
for you tonight.

00:05:22.354 --> 00:05:24.523
The very funny Ricky Gervais
is on the show.

00:05:24.523 --> 00:05:27.259
I asked Ricky what charity
he wanted to go to. He said,

00:05:27.259 --> 00:05:29.829
"I just don't want to play
a game on your show.

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:31.364
I just don't want
to play a game."

00:05:31.364 --> 00:05:35.034
And -- That's not --
That almost sounded like --

00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:37.303
Who is -- Jason...

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:39.305
Statham. I don't sound like
Ricky Gervais.

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:41.474
"Ricky Gervais
doesn't sound like that.

00:05:41.474 --> 00:05:44.476
That's more like Jason Statham,
like that.

00:05:44.476 --> 00:05:45.811
He talks like that.

00:05:45.811 --> 00:05:47.012
Yeah, what you doing?

00:05:47.012 --> 00:05:48.614
What's your name?" Jimmy?

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:51.950
"Yeah, Jimmy's not a name
for an adult man, is it?"

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:53.352
No? James?

00:05:53.352 --> 00:05:55.787
"That's better. Jim."

00:05:55.787 --> 00:05:57.457
Alright, call me Jim.

00:05:57.457 --> 00:06:00.959
"What you do?"
I'm, like, a talk-show host.

00:06:00.959 --> 00:06:04.163
"Don't really like chat shows."

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:05.530
'Cause he said that to me once.

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:08.033
But Ricky Gervais is on
the show, and he loves to laugh.

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:09.334
I love playing games with him,

00:06:09.334 --> 00:06:11.304
because he doesn't like
to play games with me.

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:13.606
So I think that's
what makes it fun.

00:06:13.606 --> 00:06:16.208
Also, gosh,

00:06:16.208 --> 00:06:20.646 line:0%
Emmy-winner, Tony-winner,
Billy Porter on the show.

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:22.247 line:0%
Actorsfund.org.

00:06:22.247 --> 00:06:23.916 line:0%
He's probably won more awards,
as well,

00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:26.452
I'm probably not listing,
but I do love Billy Porter.

00:06:26.452 --> 00:06:29.622
I will say he definitely wins
at the red carpet.

00:06:29.622 --> 00:06:31.724
I mean, that dude just scores.

00:06:31.724 --> 00:06:33.526
He's unbelievable. I love him.

00:06:33.526 --> 00:06:36.129
I mean, the hat that opens up?

00:06:36.129 --> 00:06:38.430
[ Whistles ]
That was the best move.

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:40.466
And we got great,
great, great music.

00:06:40.466 --> 00:06:41.867
Man, we love them.

00:06:41.867 --> 00:06:44.737
The Lumineers are on the show,
and we love The Lumineers.

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:47.006
Let's see, they're doing
"Salt in the Sea"

00:06:47.006 --> 00:06:48.774
from their album "III."

00:06:48.774 --> 00:06:51.710
But this is what they're doing.

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:53.780
They're working with MusiCares,

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:55.347
and they have
a COVID-19 relief fund

00:06:55.347 --> 00:06:58.250
for folks in the music community
affected by the pandemic.

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:02.621 line:0%
So you text "Lumineers"
to 41444,

00:07:02.621 --> 00:07:06.592 line:0%
or you text "Meals" to 80100.

00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:08.827 line:0%
This is the new way to donate.
Just do that.

00:07:08.827 --> 00:07:10.529 line:0%
Your phone will take care
of the rest of the stuff.

00:07:10.529 --> 00:07:11.597 line:0%
It's amazing stuff, guys.

00:07:11.597 --> 00:07:15.000 line:0%
You'll be helping
a lot of great people.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:16.869
You know, it's Tuesday.
There's no real thing

00:07:16.869 --> 00:07:19.638
of what we're actually doing on
our show. There's no set things.

00:07:19.638 --> 00:07:21.474
But now and then
we like to have a routine,

00:07:21.474 --> 00:07:23.275
but this one thing
we started doing,

00:07:23.275 --> 00:07:24.977
'cause I have no guests
and everything.

00:07:24.977 --> 00:07:28.247
And -- We do have guests, and
it's great now. It's awesome.

00:07:28.247 --> 00:07:30.249
But when we first started,
I asked my wife

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:32.150
if I could ask her
some questions,

00:07:32.150 --> 00:07:34.820
'cause she's our camera person,

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:37.789
and she does not want
to be on camera.

00:07:37.789 --> 00:07:39.826
But for this,
she'll make the exception,

00:07:39.826 --> 00:07:42.227
just 'cause we're here, we're
home, we're trying our best,

00:07:42.227 --> 00:07:45.197
we're doing our stuff.
So this is "Ask the Fallons."

00:07:45.197 --> 00:07:48.501
You had questions for me,
my daughters, my wife.

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:50.969
You had silly questions.
You had personal questions.

00:07:50.969 --> 00:07:54.140
We're down with all of them,
so, we appreciate them.

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:58.377
So now I'm going to go
for a safe walk around my house

00:07:58.377 --> 00:08:01.013
with a mask, with my wife.

00:08:01.013 --> 00:08:04.116
This is "Ask the Fallons."

00:08:04.116 --> 00:08:08.020
-♪ Ask the Fallons,
Ask the Fallons ♪

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:10.322
-Okay, here we are.
This is "Ask the Fallons."

00:08:10.322 --> 00:08:12.657
Thank you very much. You sent in
a bunch of questions.

00:08:12.657 --> 00:08:14.193
We have the masks on.

00:08:14.193 --> 00:08:16.062
-Yes.

00:08:16.062 --> 00:08:18.396
We are going to be very careful.

00:08:18.396 --> 00:08:19.998
-If we see any people,

00:08:19.998 --> 00:08:21.333
we have to put the mask --
-We're putting them on.

00:08:21.333 --> 00:08:23.268
-Yeah. I'm going
to hang one from the ear.

00:08:23.268 --> 00:08:24.770
-I'm just not going to do that.

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:27.573
-Okay.
-[ Laughs ]

00:08:27.573 --> 00:08:29.775
-Alright. Ready?
-Yeah.

00:08:29.775 --> 00:08:31.276
-Alright.

00:08:31.276 --> 00:08:33.679
Nancy, you said last week
your dream is to open a store.

00:08:33.679 --> 00:08:35.514
What kind of store?

00:08:35.514 --> 00:08:38.918
-Um, that's probably why
the dream hasn't happened yet.

00:08:38.918 --> 00:08:42.522
[ Chuckles ] No, my store
would be a treasure store,

00:08:42.522 --> 00:08:45.725
vintage, one-of-a-kind
things, gifts.

00:08:45.725 --> 00:08:49.661
Not expensive, not annoying,

00:08:49.661 --> 00:08:52.231
but just a place you could
go in and just find,

00:08:52.231 --> 00:08:54.333
like, the best painting
that you were looking for,

00:08:54.333 --> 00:08:57.736
that one-of-a-kind
original pencil holder

00:08:57.736 --> 00:09:00.373
from someone a long time ago,

00:09:00.373 --> 00:09:02.708
that kind of stuff.
Not clothing. Just --

00:09:02.708 --> 00:09:04.910
-Not new stuff?
-Not new.

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:05.978
-But a gift shop?
-Loved.

00:09:05.978 --> 00:09:07.145
Things that
have been loved before.

00:09:07.145 --> 00:09:09.114
-Oh, okay.
-Not really a gift shop,

00:09:09.114 --> 00:09:10.616
but yeah, a place you --

00:09:10.616 --> 00:09:15.621
It would probably have
a very specific customer,

00:09:15.621 --> 00:09:17.356
like me. [ Laughs ]

00:09:17.356 --> 00:09:19.825
And then I'd have to
give everything up.

00:09:19.825 --> 00:09:23.962
-How did you know you were ready
to have kids?

00:09:23.962 --> 00:09:26.432
-We were ready
when we got married.

00:09:26.432 --> 00:09:29.367
I got married later in life.

00:09:29.367 --> 00:09:33.306
And you love kids,
and I love kids.

00:09:33.306 --> 00:09:34.639
And --

00:09:34.639 --> 00:09:36.008
-That was always
the plan, right?

00:09:36.008 --> 00:09:37.076
-That was just the plan.

00:09:37.076 --> 00:09:38.878
It wasn't even a, like,
"Are you ready?"

00:09:38.878 --> 00:09:41.280
It was just, like, "Now
how are you going to do this?"

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:42.848
And that was
a whole other question.

00:09:42.848 --> 00:09:44.249
[ Laughs ]

00:09:44.249 --> 00:09:46.485
-Yeah.
-But we did it!

00:09:46.485 --> 00:09:48.554
-That was an interesting time.

00:09:48.554 --> 00:09:50.722
-Yeah. So that was
five -- five years

00:09:50.722 --> 00:09:55.060
of really, really, really,
really, really deciding

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:59.698
not to give up and to --

00:09:59.698 --> 00:10:02.835
At a certain point, it just
had to become almost like a job,

00:10:02.835 --> 00:10:05.938
'cause it's way too emotional to
live emotionally through that.

00:10:05.938 --> 00:10:08.807
So you just keep going
and going and going.

00:10:08.807 --> 00:10:10.409
And if you really
want something,

00:10:10.409 --> 00:10:11.610
you just make it happen.

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:13.946
And you have all these things
where you go,

00:10:13.946 --> 00:10:15.413
"Yeah, but I would
never do that.

00:10:15.413 --> 00:10:17.115
Yes, but I would never do that.
But I would never --

00:10:17.115 --> 00:10:19.084
And then all of a sudden,
you're like, "Hey, I'll do that.

00:10:19.084 --> 00:10:21.020
If it's for my family,
I'll do anything."

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:25.557
So I think if anyone's out there

00:10:25.557 --> 00:10:29.761
having the dream,
do not give up.

00:10:29.761 --> 00:10:32.797
Because I realize, too,
that unlike even becoming

00:10:32.797 --> 00:10:34.433
like a multi-billionaire,

00:10:34.433 --> 00:10:37.502
you can stumble upon
a lottery ticket and win it

00:10:37.502 --> 00:10:38.671
and win the lottery.

00:10:38.671 --> 00:10:41.340
But you will not ever
stumble upon a child

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:44.109
that will -- you can love
and have as your family.

00:10:44.109 --> 00:10:46.578
So don't give up.

00:10:46.578 --> 00:10:49.147
Take bad weekends.
Every time we got bad news,

00:10:49.147 --> 00:10:51.217
we would go away
for one weekend.

00:10:51.217 --> 00:10:53.685
And --
-We went away a lot.

00:10:53.685 --> 00:10:55.721
-And then we went away
a lot, yeah.

00:10:55.721 --> 00:10:58.523
And some times
were easier than others.

00:10:58.523 --> 00:11:01.127
But then we'd just get right
back -- back up.

00:11:01.127 --> 00:11:02.928
-Gosh, that was just crazy, man.

00:11:02.928 --> 00:11:05.498
That was nuts at one point.
-Yeah, it is --

00:11:05.498 --> 00:11:07.466
-It was just shots and things...

00:11:07.466 --> 00:11:08.968
-Oh, yeah.
-...and drinking weird teas.

00:11:08.968 --> 00:11:12.337
Do you remember that one?
-Oh, I cried 3, 14 times a day.

00:11:12.337 --> 00:11:13.538
-Yeah, me, too.

00:11:13.538 --> 00:11:15.207
I was --
-Just smelling this tea.

00:11:15.207 --> 00:11:17.843
-I was sleeping upside down.
I was dangling from my --

00:11:17.843 --> 00:11:20.212
from -- My feet were attached
to the ceiling.

00:11:20.212 --> 00:11:22.681
I had magnets in my underwear.

00:11:22.681 --> 00:11:24.817
-Yep, the whole --
-Still do, man.

00:11:24.817 --> 00:11:26.785
-Yeah, those magnets
are still working, I think.

00:11:26.785 --> 00:11:28.487
[ Both laugh ]

00:11:28.487 --> 00:11:29.855
-You know,
I was stuck to the fridge.

00:11:29.855 --> 00:11:32.224
I was stuck to the fridge
for four days --

00:11:32.224 --> 00:11:33.659
four days last week,
no one found me.

00:11:33.659 --> 00:11:34.826
[ Both laugh ]

00:11:34.826 --> 00:11:36.795
-Oh, that's where you were.
-Yeah.

00:11:36.795 --> 00:11:41.099
But then all the things kind of
just -- everything kind of --

00:11:41.099 --> 00:11:43.502
Opportunities come up,
and you have to, like, decide,

00:11:43.502 --> 00:11:45.003
is this the path you want to go?

00:11:45.003 --> 00:11:47.339
And, gosh, it was the best move
we ever made.

00:11:47.339 --> 00:11:49.508
-So lucky, yeah.
-We are so lucky.

00:11:49.508 --> 00:11:51.543
We have two beautiful girls.
-Yeah.

00:11:51.543 --> 00:11:53.412
-And, yeah, couldn't be --

00:11:53.412 --> 00:11:54.680
-Couldn't be happier
and more lucky

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:58.050
and more in love with them
and each other.

00:11:58.050 --> 00:12:00.051
[ Laughs ]
-They are the best things ever.

00:12:00.051 --> 00:12:01.220
Someone put on there,

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:04.189
"What advice did you take
when you had kids?"

00:12:04.189 --> 00:12:06.158
-Ooh, I know. Take no advice.

00:12:06.158 --> 00:12:07.659
-Yeah. Wait, that was my answer.

00:12:07.659 --> 00:12:09.428
-Oh, whoopsie. Uh...

00:12:09.428 --> 00:12:11.430
[ Laughter ]

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:13.599
-I would say do not take
any advice from anyone.

00:12:13.599 --> 00:12:15.935
-Yeah, listen, you'll know.
Our guts know. We know. Just --

00:12:15.935 --> 00:12:17.770
-We got so many books.
-Don't overdo it.

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:19.271
Don't -- Yeah, no,
I didn't read one book.

00:12:19.271 --> 00:12:20.940
-So many books and things.
-No, no, no.

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:23.209
-Monks raising babies and --

00:12:23.209 --> 00:12:25.044
-If you don't follow your gut...

00:12:25.044 --> 00:12:26.244
-I read a little bit
of that one.

00:12:26.244 --> 00:12:27.679
-...you're going
to lose your mind,

00:12:27.679 --> 00:12:28.981
actually quite literally,

00:12:28.981 --> 00:12:30.482
'cause you won't really
know what to do,

00:12:30.482 --> 00:12:31.817
and your instincts
won't kick in.

00:12:31.817 --> 00:12:34.252
You'll just be dulling
your instincts.

00:12:34.252 --> 00:12:35.420
No one really knows.

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:37.289
-No one knows.
-Just do the best you can.

00:12:37.289 --> 00:12:40.793
Do -- And do it from love,
and keep your sense of humor,

00:12:40.793 --> 00:12:42.861
and take deep breaths,
'cause they do help.

00:12:42.861 --> 00:12:44.430
-Should we do one more?
-Sure.

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:46.632
-If you could have dinner with
any three people, alive or dead,

00:12:46.632 --> 00:12:48.433
who would they be?

00:12:48.433 --> 00:12:50.035
I say three people's the max,

00:12:50.035 --> 00:12:51.636
no matter who they are,
alive or dead.

00:12:51.636 --> 00:12:53.605
-Yeah, he does say that.

00:12:53.605 --> 00:12:57.275
-I can only do --
I can say four.

00:12:57.275 --> 00:12:59.979
-When he gets invited to dinners
of like six people --

00:12:59.979 --> 00:13:02.013
-No, no.
-He being the sixth --

00:13:02.013 --> 00:13:04.183
-I can't do that.
It's too much work.

00:13:04.183 --> 00:13:07.686
-[ Gasps ] Oh, sorry,
bunnies everywhere.

00:13:07.686 --> 00:13:13.626
My -- I have, of course,
the long list of heroes.

00:13:13.626 --> 00:13:15.794
But the real truth to this,
it's so funny,

00:13:15.794 --> 00:13:17.929
and so I was thinking about this
the other night

00:13:17.929 --> 00:13:21.633
is I would love my mom
to have met Jimmy.

00:13:21.633 --> 00:13:24.803
So it would be my mom.

00:13:24.803 --> 00:13:26.605
Pammy Pam.

00:13:26.605 --> 00:13:28.273
-You assuming that
I'm coming to the dinner?

00:13:28.273 --> 00:13:30.542
-Yeah, it's you and Mom.
[ Both laugh ]

00:13:30.542 --> 00:13:32.912
Just Mom to talk about you,
actually.

00:13:32.912 --> 00:13:34.245
You can come for half of it.

00:13:34.245 --> 00:13:36.081
-Mom and Abraham Lincoln.
-And then I want her opinion.

00:13:36.081 --> 00:13:38.283
-Mom, Abraham Lincoln, and me.
-Abraham Lincoln, Maya Angelou,

00:13:38.283 --> 00:13:39.852
Jane Goodall, and you.

00:13:39.852 --> 00:13:41.620
And that's a good party.
-Oh, that's too many people.

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:42.754
-I'm going,
but now you won't come

00:13:42.754 --> 00:13:44.223
'cause there are
too many people there.

00:13:44.223 --> 00:13:47.393
Yeah, you got to split it up.
Me, Maya Angelou, and Lincoln.

00:13:47.393 --> 00:13:49.461
We're having our own thing,
and we'll Zoom --

00:13:49.461 --> 00:13:50.963
We'll Zoom party --
-You'll Zoom over with --

00:13:50.963 --> 00:13:52.264
-To you and your --
-Me and Mom.

00:13:52.264 --> 00:13:54.466
Mom and me.
[ Both laugh ]

00:13:54.466 --> 00:13:55.967
-Alright. Did we do it?

00:13:55.967 --> 00:13:57.736
-I think we did it.
-I think we did it.

00:13:57.736 --> 00:13:59.738
-Did our max.

00:13:59.738 --> 00:14:02.474
-That's it.
-Everybody, stay strong.

00:14:02.474 --> 00:14:04.710
-Yep. Thank you, everybody.

